From a62e2e19f60bea00b6525464d77c30427473d132 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: testuser <mainta@example.test>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 22:11:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 10/11] feat(cli): compact the context under ACP from
 providers.json settings

The ACP session config set no `compaction`, so a turn on a 1,000,000-token model never
compacted, providers.json contextWindow was inert, and the request grew to twice the
configured window with no summary call (measured against a local fake Bedrock).

The session config now takes compaction from providers.json settings.compaction
{enabled, strategy, thresholdRatio}. It is on when the model's window is known (a
configured contextWindow or a catalog window) and off when the window is a guess: an id
outside the catalog with no window would be summarised at the 128,000 fallback.
enabled: true forces it on. The strategy is agentic (a summary call to the same model,
route and credentials) or basic (truncation).

thresholdRatio replaces the fixed 0.9 in the compaction trigger (0.1 to 0.99). A count
the provider reported at exactly the threshold compacts for every estimate; the scaled
budget lost about one estimate in five to floating point. A configured contextWindow now
reaches the compaction budget of a model that is in the catalog too
(resolveModelInfoFromConfig).

A provider fault (a retryable failure, or a 401 or 403) in the agentic summary call ends
the turn with the structured error of patch 0011 (phase compaction) instead of falling
back to truncation, so the harness's failover decides; any other summary failure still
falls back to basic. The legacy done chunk and the summary error carry errorDetails.

session/prompt reports _meta.harness {compactions, compaction}: the compactions the turn
performed (mode, tokens and messages before and after) and the settings it ran with.
